  "title": "Sparta",
  "summary": "Sparta was a city-state in Laconia, in the southeast Peloponnese, formed around the 9th century BCE when villages united. It conquered neighbours, notably Messenia, and used helots as farm labour. Two hereditary kings ruled together. It led the Peloponnesian League, won the Peloponnesian War, was beaten by Thebes at Leuctra in 371 BCE, and lost independence in 195 BCE.",
